2. `TryDequeue(out T result)`: Attempts to remove and return the object at the beginning of the queue. If the operation is successful, the method returns true and sets the `result` parameter to the dequeued item. If the queue is empty, the method returns false.
3. Blocking behavior: When a thread attempts to dequeue an item from an empty queue, it should block until an item becomes available.

