You are tasked with implementing a generic class that enforces bounds on a given value. The class should allow for the attachment of event handlers to be notified when the bounds are changed. Your task is to create a new class that adheres to the provided interface and fulfills the requirements.

Your task is to create a class `BoundedValue<T>` that implements the `IBounds<T>` interface. The `IBounds<T>` interface is defined as follows:

```csharp
namespace Juce.Core.Bounds
{
    public interface IBounds<T>
    {
        event GenericEvent<IBounds<T>, EventArgs> OnBoundsChanged;
        T ApplyBounds(T value);
    }
}
```

Your `BoundedValue<T>` class should enforce bounds on a given value of type `T`. It should have the following properties and methods:

1. A constructor that takes two parameters: `minValue` and `maxValue` of type `T`, representing the lower and upper bounds, respectively.
2. A property `MinValue` of type `T` that represents the lower bound.
3. A property `MaxValue` of type `T` that represents the upper bound.
4. A property `Value` of type `T` that represents the current value, enforcing the bounds set by `MinValue` and `MaxValue`.
5. An event `OnBoundsChanged` that should be triggered whenever the bounds are changed.
6. A method `ApplyBounds` that takes a value of type `T` and enforces the bounds set by `MinValue` and `MaxValue`. If the given value is outside the bounds, it should be clamped to the nearest bound.

Ensure that the `OnBoundsChanged` event is triggered whenever the `MinValue` or `MaxValue` properties are modified.

answer:
```csharp
using System;

namespace Juce.Core.Bounds
{
    public class BoundedValue<T> : IBounds<T>
    {
        private T minValue;
        private T maxValue;
        private T value;

        public event GenericEvent<IBounds<T>, EventArgs> OnBoundsChanged;

        public BoundedValue(T minValue, T maxValue)
        {
            this.minValue = minValue;
            this.maxValue = maxValue;
            this.value = minValue; // Initialize value to the minimum bound
        }

        public T MinValue
        {
            get { return minValue; }
            set
            {
                minValue = value;
                OnBoundsChanged?.Invoke(this, EventArgs.Empty);
            }
        }

        public T MaxValue
        {
            get { return maxValue; }
            set
            {
                maxValue = value;
                OnBoundsChanged?.Invoke(this, EventArgs.Empty);
            }
        }

        public T Value
        {
            get { return value; }
            set
            {
                this.value = ApplyBounds(value);
            }
        }

        public T ApplyBounds(T value)
        {
            if (Comparer<T>.Default.Compare(value, minValue) < 0)
            {
                return minValue;
            }
            else if (Comparer<T>.Default.Compare(value, maxValue) > 0)
            {
                return maxValue;
            }
            else
            {
                return value;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This solution provides a `BoundedValue<T>` class that implements the `IBounds<T>` interface. It enforces bounds on a given value of type `T`, triggers the `OnBoundsChanged` event when the bounds are modified, and clamps the value to the nearest bound using the `ApplyBounds` method.

