```csharp
public static IEnumerable<int> Toposort1(Dictionary<int, List<int>> graph)
{
    var inDegree = new int[graph.Count];
    foreach (var neighbors in graph.Values)
    {
        foreach (var neighbor in neighbors)
        {
            inDegree[neighbor]++;
        }
    }

    var queue = new Queue<int>();
    for (int i = 0; i < inDegree.Length; i++)
    {
        if (inDegree[i] == 0)
        {
            queue.Enqueue(i);
        }
    }

    while (queue.Count > 0)
    {
        var node = queue.Dequeue();
        yield return node;

        if (graph.ContainsKey(node))
        {
            foreach (var neighbor in graph[node])
            {
                inDegree[neighbor]--;
                if (inDegree[neighbor] == 0)
                {
                    queue.Enqueue(neighbor);
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `Toposort1` method takes a dictionary representing the graph where the keys are the vertices and the values are lists of adjacent vertices. It calculates the in-degree of each vertex, initializes a queue with vertices having in-degree 0, and then performs a modified breadth-first search to yield the vertices in the topological order.

