The `RetryAssert` method repeatedly executes the `assertion` function at intervals of `retryInterval` milliseconds, up to `retryCount` times. If the `assertion` function returns `true` at any point, the method returns without any further retries. If the `assertion` function never returns `true` within the given number of retries, the method throws an `AssertionException` with the provided `failureMessage`.

