You are tasked with implementing a statistical calculation for a given dataset. The dataset consists of a series of numerical values, and you are required to calculate the standard deviation of these values. The standard deviation is a measure of the amount of variation or dispersion of a set of values. It is calculated as the square root of the average of the squared differences between each value and the mean of the dataset.

You are provided with a class `CorrelationCalculator` that contains a method `CalculateStandardDeviation` which takes in a list of numerical values and returns the standard deviation of the dataset.

The `CorrelationCalculator` class has the following structure:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace Statistics
{
    public class CorrelationCalculator
    {
        public double CalculateStandardDeviation(List<double> values)
        {
            // Your implementation goes here
        }
    }
}
```

Your task is to complete the `CalculateStandardDeviation` method to calculate the standard deviation of the given dataset.

answer:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace Statistics
{
    public class CorrelationCalculator
    {
        public double CalculateStandardDeviation(List<double> values)
        {
            if (values.Count < 2)
            {
                throw new ArgumentException("At least two values are required to calculate standard deviation.");
            }

            // Calculate the mean of the dataset
            double sum = 0;
            foreach (var value in values)
            {
                sum += value;
            }
            double mean = sum / values.Count;

            // Calculate the sum of squared differences from the mean
            double sumOfSquaredDifferences = 0;
            foreach (var value in values)
            {
                sumOfSquaredDifferences += Math.Pow(value - mean, 2);
            }

            // Calculate the variance and standard deviation
            double variance = sumOfSquaredDifferences / values.Count;
            double standardDeviation = Math.Sqrt(variance);

            return standardDeviation;
        }
    }
}
```

In the `CalculateStandardDeviation` method, the standard deviation is calculated by first finding the mean of the dataset, then computing the sum of squared differences from the mean, followed by calculating the variance and finally obtaining the standard deviation as the square root of the variance. If the input list has less than two values, an `ArgumentException` is thrown.

