public class BinaryTree
{
    public int MaxDistanceBetweenNodes(Node root)
    {
        if (root == null)
            return 0;

        int[] result = new int[1];
        MaxDepth(root, result);
        return result[0];
    }

    private int MaxDepth(Node node, int[] result)
    {
        if (node == null)
            return 0;

        int leftDepth = MaxDepth(node.Left, result);
        int rightDepth = MaxDepth(node.Right, result);

        result[0] = Math.Max(result[0], leftDepth + rightDepth);

        return Math.Max(leftDepth, rightDepth) + 1;
    }
}
```

The `MaxDistanceBetweenNodes` method uses a helper function `MaxDepth` to calculate the maximum depth of the tree while updating the maximum distance between nodes as it traverses the tree. This approach ensures an efficient solution with a time complexity of O(n), where n is the number of nodes in the binary tree.

