public static void Adpcm2toPcm16(byte[] inputBytes, short[] pcm16, ref int last1, ref int penult1)
{
    int stepIndex = 0;
    int diff = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < 16; i += 2)
    {
        int sample1 = inputBytes[i / 2] & 0x0F;
        int sample2 = (inputBytes[i / 2] >> 4) & 0x0F;

        diff = stepTable[stepIndex] >> 3;
        if ((sample1 & 1) == 1) diff += stepTable[stepIndex];
        if ((sample1 & 2) == 2) diff += stepTable[stepIndex] >> 1;
        if ((sample1 & 4) == 4) diff += stepTable[stepIndex] >> 2;
        if ((sample1 & 8) == 8) diff += stepTable[stepIndex] >> 3;

        pcm16[i] = (short)Math.Max(-32768, Math.Min(32767, last1 + diff));
        last1 = pcm16[i];

        stepIndex += indexTable[sample1];
        stepIndex = Math.Max(0, Math.Min(88, stepIndex));

        diff = stepTable[stepIndex] >> 3;
        if ((sample2 & 1) == 1) diff += stepTable[stepIndex];
        if ((sample2 & 2) == 2) diff += stepTable[stepIndex] >> 1;
        if ((sample2 & 4) == 4) diff += stepTable[stepIndex] >> 2;
        if ((sample2 & 8) == 8) diff += stepTable[stepIndex] >> 3;

        pcm16[i + 1] = (short)Math.Max(-32768, Math.Min(32767, last1 + diff));
        last1 = pcm16[i + 1];

        stepIndex += indexTable[sample2];
        stepIndex = Math.Max(0, Math.Min(88, stepIndex));
    }

    penult1 = pcm16[14];
}
```

In the provided solution, the `Adpcm2toPcm16` function decodes the input ADPCM data into a 16-bit PCM array using the ADPCM decoding algorithm. The function iterates through the input bytes, applies the decoding algorithm, and stores the decoded PCM samples in the `pcm16` array. The `last1` and `penult1` variables are updated as the decoding progresses. The `stepTable` and `indexTable` arrays are assumed to be predefined lookup tables used in the ADPCM decoding algorithm.

