PascalABC.NET does not natively support Hadoop MapReduce as it is platform-dependent and heavily dependent on Java. However, you can use the .NET SDK for Hadoop (Microsoft.Hadoop.MapReduce) to write MapReduce jobs in PascalABC.NET for Hadoop, in Azure environments particularly. Here's a possible PascalABC.NET conversion in Microsoft Hadoop SDK:

```csharp
using Microsoft.Hadoop.MapReduce;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class WordCount
{
    public class TokenizeMapper : MapperBase
    {
        public override void Map(string inputLine, MapperContext context)
        {
            char[] delimiterChars = { ' ', '\t' };
            string[] words = inputLine.Split(delimiterChars);

            foreach (string word in words)
            {
                if(!string.IsNullOrEmpty(word))
                {
                    context.EmitKeyValue(word.ToLower(), "1");
                } 
            }
        }
    }

    public class IntSumReducer : ReducerCombinerBase
    {
        public override void Reduce(string key, IEnumerable<string> values, ReducerCombinerContext context)
        {
            int wordCount = 0;

            foreach (var value in values)
            {
                wordCount += int.Parse(value);
            }

            context.EmitKeyValue(key, wordCount.ToString());
        }
    }

    public class WordCountJob : HadoopJob<TokenizeMapper, IntSumReducer> { }

    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            var hadoop = Hadoop.Connect();
            var result = hadoop.MapReduceJob.Execute<WordCountJob>();

            if (result.Info.ExitCode != 0)
            {
                System.Console.WriteLine("Job failed!");
            }
            else
            {
                System.Console.WriteLine("Job succeeded!");
            }
        }
    }
}
```
In this code, MapperBase, ReducerCombinerBase, and HadoopJob<TMapper, TReducer> are classes provided by the Microsoft.Hadoop.MapReduce namespace. It provides functionality similar to what Hadoop MapReduce provides in Java.

However, you will need a Hadoop cluster running on Azure and the Microsoft Azure SDK to execute this .NET MapReduce job.

