Here is a simple PascalABC.NET program that can remove consecutive duplicate characters from a given string:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        string str = "azxxzy";

        // Call the function to erase duplicate chars
        string result = RemoveDuplicates(str);

        // Print the result
        Console.WriteLine("Input: " + str);
        Console.WriteLine("Output: " + result);

        Console.ReadKey();
    }

    static string RemoveDuplicates(string str)
    {
        // If the string is null or only consists of 1 character just return it
        if (str == null || str.Length <= 1)
            return str;

        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();

        // Start with the first character
        char prevChar = str[0];
        result.Append(prevChar);

        // Loop through the rest of the characters
        for (int i = 1; i < str.Length; i++)
        {
            // If the current character does not equal the previous character, append it to the result
            if (str[i] != prevChar)
            {
                result.Append(str[i]);
                prevChar = str[i]; // Update the previous character
            }
        }

        return result.ToString(); 
    }
}
```

When you run this program, it will print:

```bash
Input: azxxzy
Output: azxzy
```

This program works by looping through each character in the input string and comparing it to the previous character. If the current character is different, it gets appended to the result. This effectually eradicates any duplicate consecutive characters.

