Here's a simple way you can try to exchange placeholder image in Openxml,
Let's say you have identified your placeholder image with a tag say {image}. Now you can replace it with another image with the following approach.

1) First make sure you have installed the DocumentFormat.OpenXml libray in your project. Use this command in Nuget package manager console to install

```csharp
Install-Package DocumentFormat.OpenXml
```

2) Now Proceed to replace the placeholder:

```csharp
using DocumentFormat.OpenXml.Packaging;
using DocumentFormat.OpenXml.Wordprocessing;

public void ReplaceImage(string docxFile, string newImage)
{
      using (WordprocessingDocument wordDoc = WordprocessingDocument.Open(docxFile, true))
       {
           MainDocumentPart mainPart = wordDoc.MainDocumentPart;

           // Get the image part by tag
           ImagePart imagePart = (ImagePart)mainPart.Document.Body.Descendants<Tag>().Where(t => t.Val.Value.Equals("{image}")).FirstOrDefault().Parent.ChildElements.FirstOrDefault(e => e is Drawing).Descendants<ImagePart>().FirstOrDefault();

           if (imagePart != null)
           {
               // Delete the old image.
               mainPart.DeletePart(imagePart);

               // Add a new image part.
               ImagePart newImagePart = mainPart.AddImagePart(ImagePartType.Jpeg);

               // Copy the image to the new image part.
               using (FileStream stream = new FileStream(newImage, FileMode.Open))
               {
                   newImagePart.FeedData(stream);
               }
           }
       }
}
```

In the code above in place of "{image}", please replace it with your own placeholder tag. This function will take in two parameters, docxFile the path to your word document, and newImage the path to your new image. It will then replace all images in the document that have the tag specified.

This is only a basic example and doesn't account for edge-cases such as what should happen if no image or many images have the specified tag.

Note - This only covers how to replace images not how to make sure that the images are resized appropriately to fit the space available.

