}
```
In above example, the `GetChildrenByParentId` method in `YourDataAccess` class will accept `parentId` and get all related children entity. This approach avoids potential infinite loops because you are explicitly controlling when and how related entities are loaded. 

Please note that in `TEntityChild` class, the association is only to the parent and there is no reference to child collection to prevent infinite loop. In many-many scenario where TEntity contains collection of TEntityChild and each TEntityChild has reference to TEntity, it is difficult to ensure the loading does not fall into infinite loop. Forcing manually loading of related entities can be a more reliable approach.

