An important thing to understand when doing AJAX with ASP.NET WebForms is, that AJAX is not really removing postbacks, but more or less hiding them. The UpdatePanel for example works by intercepting the postback event, cancelling the original postback and then manually performing a postback. The server then only sends back the content of the UpdatePanel, causing it to look like a partial page update. 

