Here is how you can create a program that performs these actions in PascalABC.NET. We simply iterate over each character of the input strings, convert them to their ASCII values using the built-in method, and then concatenate the results. Reverse process is performed in the decoding function.

```PascalABC.NET
using System;
using System.Text;

class StringEncoder{

    static void Main(string[] args){
        string str1 = "hello";
        string str2 = "world";

        string encodedString = Encode(str1, str2);
        Console.WriteLine("Encoded string: " + encodedString);

        Tuple<string, string> originalStrings = Decode(encodedString);
        Console.WriteLine("Decoded strings: " 
                        + originalStrings.Item1 
                        + ", " 
                        + originalStrings.Item2);
    }

    public static string Encode(string str1, string str2){
        StringBuilder encodedStr1 = new StringBuilder();
        StringBuilder encodedStr2 = new StringBuilder();

        foreach (char ch in str1)
            encodedStr1.Append((int)ch);
        foreach (char ch in str2)
            encodedStr2.Append((int)ch);

        return encodedStr1.ToString() + encodedStr2.ToString();
    }

    public static Tuple<string, string> Decode(string encodedStr){
        StringBuilder decodedStr1 = new StringBuilder();
        StringBuilder decodedStr2 = new StringBuilder();
        bool isSecond = false;
        for (int i = 0; i < encodedStr.Length; i += 3){
            int code = int.Parse(encodedStr.Substring(i, 3));
            if(code >= 97 && code <= 122 && !isSecond){
                decodedStr1.Append((char)code);
            } else if(code >= 97 && code <= 122 && isSecond){
                decodedStr2.Append((char)code);
            } else {
                isSecond = true;
                i -= 1;
                continue;
            }
        }
        return new Tuple<string, string>(decodedStr1.ToString(), decodedStr2.ToString());
    }
}
```

Please note that this program assumes that all ASCII codes are 3 digits long and every string to be encoded consists only of lower case letters. You should add error checking and handling mechanisms according to your specific requirements.

The built-in `Tuple` class in PascalABC.NET is used to return both decoded strings from the Decode function.

