Unfortunately, as of the time of writing, there's no documented method to directly manipulate the properties of a NewWindow such as width, height, or position in WebView2. However, there are ways to work around this.

First, we can use the `NewWindowRequested` event handler. We can create our own window and navigate it to the URL supplied in the event arguments. Here's an example of how you might do this:

```csharp
private void webView_CoreWebView2_NewWindowRequested(object sender, CoreWebView2NewWindowRequestedEventArgs e)
{
    // Suppress the automatic new window creation
    e.Handled = true;

    // Create a new form (which can be sized and positioned as you want)
    var newForm = new Form();
    newForm.Width = 800;  // Set the width
    newForm.Height = 600;  // Set the height
    newForm.StartPosition = FormStartPosition.Manual;  // Enable manual positioning
    newForm.Left = 100;  // Set the X position
    newForm.Top = 100;  // Set the Y position

    // Create a new WebView2 control
    var newWebView = new WebView2{Dock = DockStyle.Fill};

    // Wait for the CoreWebView2 initialization
    newWebView.CoreWebView2InitializationCompleted += (sender, e) => {
        // Navigate the new WebView2 control to the requested URI
        newWebView.CoreWebView2.Navigate(e.Uri);
    };

    // Add the new WebView2 control to the new form
    newForm.Controls.Add(newWebView);

    // Show the new form
    newForm.Show();

    // Assign the new WebView2 control as target window
    // Note: this step is important. It will prevent another popup and instead, use the current created form
    e.NewWindow = newWebView.CoreWebView2;
}
```

This code will create a new form and WebView2 control whenever a new window is requested. The new window's properties (such as width, height, and position) can be controlled by manipulating the new form's properties. When we set `e.Handled` to `true`, it suppresses the automatic new window creation, and when we set `e.NewWindow`, it informs the CoreWebView2 environment that this is the WebView2 we want to use for the new window.

