1. Firstly, create a custom attribute class using ActionFilterAttribute:
```csharp
public class EncryptionFilterAttribute : ActionFilterAttribute
{
    private readonly IEncryptionService _encryptionService;

    public EncryptionFilterAttribute(IEncryptionService encryptionService)
    {
        _encryptionService = encryptionService;
    }

    public override void OnActionExecuting(ActionExecutingContext context)
    {
        // This is where you need to implement decryption logic
        var encryptedModel = context.ActionArguments.First().Value; 
        var decryptedModel = _encryptionService.Decrypt(encryptedModel);

        // Replacing the encrypted model with a decrypted one
        context.ActionArguments[context.ActionArguments.First().Key] = decryptedModel;

        base.OnActionExecuting(context);
    }
}
```

2. You need to configure Dependency Injection for your Encryption Service in startup.cs.
```csharp
services.AddScoped<IEncryptionService, EncryptionService>();
```

3. Finally, in your controller, use the custom attribute:
```csharp
[EncryptionFilter]
public IActionResult YourAction([FromBody] YourModel model)
{
    // Now your model comes in already decrypted.
    // Your-existing-controller-logic
}
```

The above-mentioned steps cover the decryption part on the server side.

