Here is an algorithm implemented in PascalABC.NET to compute factorial of large numbers where the result is stored in an array instead of an integer. It includes error checking to ensure the input number is a non-negative integer. 

This code multiplies each digit starting from the Least Significant Digit (LSD), carries any overflow to the next digit, and continues this process towards the Most Significant Digit (MSD). The result is stored in reverse order i.e. MSD at the end and LSD at the start.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class FactorialProgram
{
    static List<int> CalculateFactorial(int n)
    {
        if (n < 0)
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("Input must be a non-negative integer");
        }

        List<int> result = new List<int> {1}; // Initialize result as 1

        for (int x = 2; x <= n; x++)
        {
            int carry = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < result.Count; i++)
            {
                int temp = result[i] * x + carry;
                // Determine carry for next iteration
                carry = temp / 10;
                // Store the result
                result[i] = temp % 10;
            }

            // Push carry to result while there is one
            while (carry != 0)
            {
                result.Add(carry % 10);
                carry = carry / 10;
            }
        }

        // Since the computation was done in reverse, reverse the list to get the correct representation
        result.Reverse();
        return result;
    }

    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        int num = 5;  // Change this as you wish.
        List<int> factorial = CalculateFactorial(num);

        Console.WriteLine(string.Join("", factorial.ToArray()));
    }
}
```

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n^2) and the space complexity is O(n), as the number of digits in n! is approximately equal to n.

