Scintilla control does not automatically support code folding for custom lexers, you will need to actually tell it where to add fold points in your document manually when using a custom lexer. 

Basic code folding for `{` and `}` can be achieved by updating fold levels for each line. Here's some simple code that might hopefully give you a starting point for your code. 

Code snippet could be something like this:

```csharp
private void MyScintilla_TextChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    // clear all folding
    myScintilla.NativeInterface.SetProperty("fold", "1");
    myScintilla.NativeInterface.SetProperty("fold.compact", "0");

    for (int i = 0; i < myScintilla.Lines.Count; i++)
    {
        var curLevel = i == 0 ? 1024 : myScintilla.Lines[i - 1].FoldLevel & (ScintillaNET.FoldLevel.NumberMask | ScintillaNET.FoldLevel.HeaderFlag);

        // new block opens "{" => increase fold level
        if (myScintilla.Lines[i].Text.Contains("{"))
        {
            curLevel++;
        }

        // block ends "}" => decrease fold level
        if (i != 0 && myScintilla.Lines[i].Text.Contains("}"))
        {
            curLevel--;
        }

        myScintilla.Lines[i].FoldLevel = (ScintillaNET.FoldLevel)curLevel;

        // set header flag
        if ((myScintilla.Lines[i].FoldLevel & ScintillaNET.FoldLevel.HeaderFlag) != 0)
        {
            myScintilla.Lines[i].FoldLevel |= ScintillaNET.FoldLevel.HeaderFlag;
        }
    }
}
```
You must attach `TextChanged` to this function like so `myScintilla.TextChanged += MyScintilla_TextChanged;`

Take note that this code is quite naïve and will not correctly handle many edge cases such as `{` or `}` appearing within strings or comments, or multiple `{` or `}` characters on the same line. Depending on your language's syntax, you may need much more complex logic to handle folding correctly, but this should give you a starting point. To correctly handle more complex scenarios, you may need to integrate more deeply with your custom lexer to determine where to place fold points based on the actual syntax of your language.

