There could be several reasons why the rollback might not work when calling the COM+ object from a .NET application. Here are a few possible causes and solutions:

1. Transaction Scope: Be sure that the .NET application is calling the COM+ component within a TransactionScope, and that it is set up to handle exceptions correctly. Transactions in COM+ components will not automatically roll back unless they are notified that an error has occurred. To do this, you need to use the System.Transaction namespace in the .NET application, and declare and use TransactionScope. Whenever an exception occurs, you need to make sure you are rolling back the transaction as well. 

Advice: 

