{
    try
    {
        // your code here
        scope.Complete();
    }
    catch(Exception)
    {
        // your error handling here
    }
}
```

2. Configuration: Ensure that your COM+ component has been configured correctly to take part in transactions. Check that the attribute "Transaction" is set to "Required" in the properties page of the COM+ component in the Component Services admin tool on your machine.

3. COM+ from ASP vs .NET: The reason it might work from your old ASP code is because in-process components (COM+ components loaded in the same process as your ASP code) can participate in automatic transaction management. .NET transactions do not automatically propagate to COM+ components, so you need to manually ensure that the COM+ component is part of the same transaction scope.

