answer:
Here is the PascalABC.NET equivalent for your code:

```CSharp
using System;

public class Solution {
    public int GetMaxTriples(int n) {
        // Generate array
        int[] arr = new int[n];
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            arr[i-1] = i * i - i + 1;
        }

        // Frequency of numbers modulo 3
        int[] freq = new int[3];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            freq[arr[i] % 3]++;
        }

        // Counting the number of triples
        int ans = 0;
        ans += freq[0]*(freq[0]-1)*(freq[0]-2)/6; // 3 numbers are from 0
        ans += freq[1]*freq[2]*(freq[0]); // one number from 0 and one from 1 and 2
        ans += freq[1]*(freq[1]-1)*(freq[1]-2)/6; // 3 numbers from 1
        ans += freq[2]*(freq[2]-1)*(freq[2]-2)/6; // 3 numbers from 2
        ans += freq[0]*(freq[0]-1)/2*freq[1]; // two numbers from 0 and one number from 1
        ans += freq[0]*(freq[0]-1)/2*freq[2]; // two numbers from 0 and one number from 2

        return ans;
    }

    public static void Main() {
        Solution soln = new Solution();
        Console.WriteLine(soln.GetMaxTriples(5));  // expected result: 1
    }
}
```
Please note that the output to the console is achieved through `Console.WriteLine()` in PascalABC.NET. The call to this method replaces the `System.out.println()` in Java.

