blah.prop1="foo";
blah.prop2="bar";



In a very generic way.  The thing I don't know how to do is take the string `prop1` in the config file and turn that into the actual property accessor in the code.  Are there any meta-programming facilities in PascalABC.NET to allow that?

answer:
Yes, PascalABC.NET has strong capabilities in reflection, which can allow this kind of meta-programming. Specifically, you'll be using classes in the `System.Reflection` namespace.

Here's an approach you can use.

```csharp
public static object CreateClassInstance(string className, Dictionary<string, string> props)
{
    // Load the type
    Type type = Type.GetType(className);

    // Create an instance of that type
    object classInstance = Activator.CreateInstance(type);

    // For each property we were given, set the value on the new instance
    foreach (KeyValuePair<string, string> entry in props)
    {
        PropertyInfo propInfo = type.GetProperty(entry.Key);
        if (propInfo != null)
        {
            propInfo.SetValue(classInstance, Convert.ChangeType(entry.Value, propInfo.PropertyType), null);
        }
    }

    return classInstance;
}
```

Here's a quick explanation of the steps:

1. `Type.GetType(string)` is used to find a `Type` instance given the name of a type. You'll need the fully-qualified name of the type, meaning you also need the namespace. So if your classes are under a `MyApplication` namespace, `className` would need to be something like "MyApplication.class1".

2. `Activator.CreateInstance(Type)` is used to create a new instance of a type.

3. `Type.GetProperty(string)` is used to get a `PropertyInfo` object which represents a particular property of the type. This property can be used to both get and set the value of that property on an instance of the type.

4. `PropertyInfo.SetValue(object, object)` is used to set the value of the property on a particular instance. The object we just created serves as the instance. It takes in the object on which you want to set the property value, and the value to set it to.

5. `Convert.ChangeType(object, Type)` is used to convert the string value from config file to the actual type of the property. This would handle conversion to basic types like integers, boolean etc.

