Below is a PascalABC.NET recursive function named "CalculatePrimeProduct" calculating the product of all prime numbers less than or equal to n:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Numerics;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        int n = 50;

        Console.WriteLine(CalculatePrimeProduct(n));

        static BigInteger CalculatePrimeProduct(int number, int i = 2, BigInteger product = 1)
        {
            if (i > number)
            {
                return product;
            }
            else if (IsPrime(i))
            {
                product *= i;
            }

            return CalculatePrimeProduct(number, i + 1, product);
        }

        static bool IsPrime(int n) 
        {
            if (n <= 1) return false;
            if (n == 2) return true;
            if (n % 2 == 0) return false;

            for (int i = 3; i * i <= n; i += 2)
            {
                if (n % i == 0)
                    return false;
            }

            return true;
        }
    }
}
```

The function "CalculatePrimeProduct" takes three arguments; number (n), i (the current number to be checked) and product (the product of prime numbers found so far). It checks if the current number (i) is prime. If it's prime, the function multiplies the prime number with the product. It continues to call itself while incrementing the current number (i) until it's greater than the given number (n).

