```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq;

namespace UnicodeStringInversion
{
    class Program
    {
        public static void Main()
        {
            string greeting = "Hello World";
            string reversed = ReverseAndTransform(greeting);
            Console.WriteLine(reversed);
        }

        public static string ReverseAndTransform(string str)
        {
            string reversed = new string(str.Reverse().ToArray());
            return string.Join(" ", reversed.Select(c => ((int)c).ToString("X2")));
        }
    }
}
```

In this script, the method `ReverseAndTransform` does the main job. It first reverses the given string using LINQ's `Reverse` function. Then it transforms the reversed string into a sequence of hexadecimal Unicode values. It does this by using the `Select` function to convert each character into its Unicode value with `((int)c)`, and then into a hexadecimal string with `ToString("X2")`. The "X2" format specifier means to represent the number as a hexadecimal string with at least two characters. Then the hexadecimal strings are joined into a single string with space as the separator using `string.Join`.

