// Do some commands
invoker.Invoke(new AddListItemCommand(list, item));
invoker.Invoke(new MoveListItemCommand(list1, item, list2));

// Oops something went wrong, undo the last command
invoker.UndoLastCommand();

// Or loop Undo-ing all commands if you have to
```

With this structure, you can independently develop new Command types and add them to the Invoker. It may take a bit more structuring (especially if you have a lot of types of Commands), but it can make your code much cleaner and easier to maintain. There are also several variations of this pattern, so you can adjust it to your specific needs.

