If you require a consistent hash value, you will need to utilize a custom hashing algorithm that provides consistent results across different environments.

One approach might be to use SHA256, or a similar algorithm, which will consistently generate the same hash for the same input string no matter what environment it's run in, at the cost of taking up more space or computational time. Here's an example:

```csharp
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Text;

public string CalculateSHA256Hash(string input)
{
    SHA256 sha256 = SHA256.Create();
    byte[] inputBytes = Encoding.ASCII.GetBytes(input);
    byte[] hashBytes = sha256.ComputeHash(inputBytes);

    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
