In the function `GenerateMultiplicationTable()`, the multiplication operation (*) is done only once for every iteration. Before, the multiplication was happening twice - once for calculating the value and second time for displaying it. Thus, the time complexity is reduced from O(2n) to O(n) which is a favourable improvement. 

For space complexity, the use of an array may increase the space requirement for very large inputs, however, for the sake of a multiplication table which conventionally goes up to 10 only, it wouldn't be a noticeable increase. Thus, it is a reasonable trade-off for the time complexity improvement.

Please note that this code only considers inputs within the limits of a PascalABC.NET int (32 bits). For larger inputs, data type of `number` should be changed to long or appropriate as per requirement, but the principle remains the same.

