Unfortunately, direct interactions with Project Server 2003 (creating tasks, projects, etc.) programmatically are not well-documented, and Microsoft has notably reduced the amount of accessible documentation available online over the years due to the version's age.

However, Microsoft Project Server 2003 does support a set of SOAP-based APIs (Project Data Service, or PDS), which allows interactions.

Here's a simple example (in PascalABC.NET) of connecting to Project Server and retrieving project list:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Xml;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        ProjectServerWebService.Project pjWebService = new ProjectServerWebService.Project();
        pjWebService.Url = "http://YourServer/ProjectServer/_vti_bin/psi/Project.asmx";
