The following is a corrected and enhanced version of your original code.

This solution focuses on making use of the ConcurrentBag class to handle concurrency when counting the number of occurrences. Also, tasks are created to handle multiple value checking tasks as requested and the result is returned in a dictionary with corresponding counts.

```PascalABC.NET
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using System.Collections.Concurrent;

public class NumOccurrenceCounter
{
    private ConcurrentBag<int> countBag = new ConcurrentBag<int>();

    public Dictionary<int, int> CheckValues(int[] arr, int[] valuesToCheck)
    {
        var results = new Dictionary<int, int>();

        var tasks = valuesToCheck.Select(valueToCheck => Task.Factory.StartNew(() =>
        {
            foreach (var num in arr)
            {
                if (num == valueToCheck)
                {
                    countBag.Add(valueToCheck);
                }
            }
        })).ToArray();

        Task.WaitAll(tasks);

        foreach (var value in valuesToCheck)
        {
            results[value] = countBag.Count(v => v == value);
        }

        return results;
    }
}

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        int[] valuesToCheck = { 7, 9 };
        int[] arr = { 1, 4, 7, 9, 7, 6, 8, 7 };
        var counter = new NumOccurrenceCounter();
        var result = counter.CheckValues(arr, valuesToCheck);

        foreach (var keyValue in result)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Number {keyValue.Key} occurs {keyValue.Value} time(s).");
        }
    }
}
```
In this code, a CheckValues method is implemented, which creates a new task for each value that we want to check in the array. Each task loops through the entire array, adds the value to the countBag whenever it's present in the array. Once all tasks have completed, the count of each checked value in the countBag is calculated and returned in a Dictionary object, where the key is the checked value and the value is its count in the array. 

The use of the ConcurrentBag and the WaitAll statement on the set of tasks guarantees thread-safety and correct results even in a multi-threaded scenario.

